      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "The permittee or owner/operator shall submit a written closure and post closure plan to the permitting authority 180 days prior to the closure date.",
      "affected_purpose": "B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Whether closure is planned or underway determines if this written submission obligation was applicable during the evaluated period and whether associated post-closure duties were in effect."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "A discussion of how the leachate collection system will be operated and maintained for three years after the surface disposal site closes if it has a liner and leachate collection system.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "The conditional phrase 'if it has a liner and leachate collection system' governs whether leachate-related operation, maintenance, and evidentiary expectations apply; different interpretations of site configuration change whether monitoring or documentation was required versus conditionally not required."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "A description of the system used to monitor continuously for methane gas in the air in any structures within the surface disposal site. The methane gas concentration shall not exceed 25% of the lower explosive limit for methane gas for three years after the sewage sludge unit closes.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B",
      "computation_change_reason": "This passage establishes both continuous methane monitoring in structures and an enforceable numeric ceiling (25% of the lower explosive limit); interpretation of which structures qualify and whether the three-year post-closure period applies changes applicable limits and monitoring obligations."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "A description of the system used to monitor for methane gas in the air at the property line of the site shall be included. The methane gas concentration at the surface disposal site property line shall not exceed the lower explosive limit for methane gas for three years after the sewage sludge unit closes.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Property-line methane monitoring carries a distinct numeric limit (the lower explosive limit) and location scope; whether this obligation applies and how property-line measurements are identified changes limit applicability and required monitoring."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "for three years after the sewage sludge unit closes",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "The post-closure three-year window defines when methane and related post-closure duties are operative; different interpretations of closure date or whether closure occurred during Federal FY2025 change which monitoring was required and how missing or non-numeric results should be classified."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "page 14, section part_i",
      "exact_span": "The run-off collection system for an active sewage sludge unit shall have the capacity to handle run-off from a 25-year, 24-hour storm event.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Whether this design-capacity standard is treated as an enforceable numeric compliance criterion for an active unit, and whether the unit was active during the evaluated period, affects whether runoff-related measurements or evidence bear on limit exceedance and monitoring obligations."
    }
  ]
}
